{
  "cells": [
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "# KV Cache, Flash Attention & Inference Optimization Notebook\n\n> Hands-on Build It and Exercises."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "## Build It"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "See `code/main.py`. We implement:"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "1. A naive `O(N\u00b2)` incremental decoder."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "2. A `O(N)` KV-cached decoder."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "3. A tiled softmax that simulates Flash Attention's running-max algorithm."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "### Step 1: KV cache"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```python"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "class KVCache:"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    def __init__(self, n_layers, n_heads, d_head):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        self.K = [[[] for _ in range(n_heads)] for _ in range(n_layers)]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        self.V = [[[] for _ in range(n_heads)] for _ in range(n_layers)]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    def append(self, layer, head, k, v):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        self.K[layer][head].append(k)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        self.V[layer][head].append(v)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    def read(self, layer, head):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        return self.K[layer][head], self.V[layer][head]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "Simple: keep growing per-token K, V vectors in per-layer, per-head lists."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "### Step 2: tiled softmax"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```python"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "def tiled_softmax_dot(q, K, V, tile=4):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    \"\"\"Flash-attention-style softmax(qK^T)V with running max/sum.\"\"\""
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    m = float(\"-inf\")"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    s = 0.0"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    out = [0.0] * len(V[0])"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    for start in range(0, len(K), tile):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        k_block = K[start:start + tile]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        v_block = V[start:start + tile]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        scores = [sum(qi * ki for qi, ki in zip(q, k)) for k in k_block]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        new_m = max(m, *scores)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        exp_old = math.exp(m - new_m) if m != float(\"-inf\") else 0.0"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        exp_new = [math.exp(sc - new_m) for sc in scores]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        s = s * exp_old + sum(exp_new)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        for j in range(len(out)):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "            out[j] = out[j] * exp_old + sum(e * v[j] for e, v in zip(exp_new, v_block))"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        m = new_m"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    return [o / s for o in out]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "Bit-identical output to `softmax(qK) V` in one shot, but at any time the working set is a `tile \u00d7 d_head` block, not the full `N \u00d7 d_head`."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "### Step 3: compare naive vs cached decoding on 100-token generation"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "Count attention operations. Naive: `O(N\u00b2)` = 5050. Cached: `O(N)` = 100. The code prints both."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "## Exercises"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "1. **Easy.** Run `code/main.py`. Confirm the naive and cached decoders produce the same output; note the op-count difference.\n2. **Medium.** Implement prefix caching: given a prompt P and several completions, run one forward pass over P to fill the KV cache, then branch per-completion. Measure speedup vs re-encoding P for each.\n3. **Hard.** Implement a toy PagedAttention: KV cache in fixed 16-token blocks with a free-list. When a sequence finishes, return its blocks to the pool. Simulate 1,000 chat completions with varying lengths. Compare memory fragmentation vs contiguous allocation."
      ]
    }
  ],
